<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Interfluent" description="Read the Interfluent privacy policy." canonical="/privacy/">
<Fragment slot="head"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/pages/privacy.css" /></Fragment>
<article class="privacy_privacy_article is-first-section"><div class="privacy_privacy_div">LEGAL</div><h1 class="privacy_privacy_h1">Privacy policy</h1><div class="privacy_privacy_div-2">Last updated September 2026 · <a href="/terms/">Terms of service</a></div><div class="privacy_privacy_div-3"><h2 class="privacy_privacy_h2">What we collect</h2><p class="privacy_privacy_p">When you request beta access or contact us, we store the name, work email, company, role and message you give us. When you connect a codebase during a pilot, we process the repositories and documents you authorise.</p><h2 class="privacy_privacy_h2-2">How we use it</h2><p class="privacy_privacy_p-2">To reply to you, run your pilot and improve Interfluent. We do not train models on your code or documents. We do not sell personal data.</p><h2 class="privacy_privacy_h2-3">Where it lives</h2><p class="privacy_privacy_p-3">Encrypted at rest and in transit. Enterprise customers may run Interfluent inside their own cloud, in which case their code never leaves it.</p><h2 class="privacy_privacy_h2-4">Your choices</h2><p class="privacy_privacy_p-4">Ask us to export or delete anything we hold about you at <a href="mailto:privacy@codelens.ai">privacy@codelens.ai</a>. We answer within 30 days.</p><p class="privacy_privacy_p-5">This is placeholder policy text for design review. Replace with counsel-reviewed copy before launch.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
